  "solution": {
    "approach": "Print multiplication table from 1 to limit for given multiplicand.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(limit)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int limit, m;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %d\", &limit, &m) == 2) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= limit; i++) {\n            printf(\"%d * %d = %d\\n\", i, m, i * m);\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int limit, m;\n    if (cin >> limit >> m) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= limit; i++) {\n            cout << i << \" * \" << m << \" = \" << i * m << \"\\n\";\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            int limit = sc.nextInt(), m = sc.nextInt();\n            for (int i = 1; i <= limit; i++) {\n                System.out.println(i + \" * \" + m + \" = \" + (i * m));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    parts = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if len(parts) >= 2:\n        limit, m = int(parts[0]), int(parts[1])\n        for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n            print(f\"{i} * {m} = {i * m}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const parts = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (parts.length >= 2) {\n        const limit = parseInt(parts[0], 10), m = parseInt(parts[1], 10);\n        for (let i = 1; i <= limit; i++) {\n            console.log(`${i} * ${m} = ${i * m}`);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Input contains limit and multiplicand. Loop i from 1 to limit and print 'i * multiplicand = product'."
  },
